1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,490
America just voted.

2
00:00:01,620 --> 00:00:02,840
AI stocks just fell.

3
00:00:02,860 --> 00:00:03,490
Connected?

4
00:00:03,510 --> 00:00:08,420
Tuesday, Democrats won the House and Senate, AP says, with a few races still counting.

5
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:11,090
Thursday, the Nasdaq fell five and a half percent.

6
00:00:11,240 --> 00:00:16,250
So why? Reason one: AI lives in giant computer warehouses, called data centers.

7
00:00:16,340 --> 00:00:19,120
Investors fear the election could slow building them.

8
00:00:19,140 --> 00:00:21,280
Fewer data centers, fewer chips sold.

9
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:24,170
Like a brick maker hearing the town might stop new houses.

10
00:00:24,350 --> 00:00:28,670
Reason two: big tech is spending huge sums on AI, and profits look slower.

11
00:00:28,690 --> 00:00:32,020
Like a lemonade stand that's worth less once sales slow down.

12
00:00:32,040 --> 00:00:34,590
Reason three: worry about higher interest rates.

13
00:00:34,760 --> 00:00:37,910
Safe savings pay more, so some money leaves risky stocks.

14
00:00:37,930 --> 00:00:41,500
Like kids leaving the candy line when the ice-cream truck shows up.

15
00:00:41,530 --> 00:00:43,160
So, did the election cause it?

16
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:45,400
Partly. It was Thursday's spark.

17
00:00:45,420 --> 00:00:47,790
But the slide started before anyone voted.

18
00:00:48,110 --> 00:00:49,980
Connected? Yes. But not the whole story.

19
00:00:50,160 --> 00:00:51,190
Follow for more.
